AI TRIP-PLANNER AGENT (intentionally not wired — honest disclosure)
  The web page also mounts the opt-in <AITripPlannerLLMAgent/> shared surface, which "renders only
  when ai_mode is local|cloud and the trip-planner-llm-agent feature toggle is on" and "stays absent
  and emits zero DOM in off mode … The baseline form below is the canonical, deterministic view"
  (TripPlannerPage.tsx L121-135). It is (a) NOT one of the 41 manifest parity items, (b) a separate
  parity unit with its own prompt + ledger row, and (c) dependent on the AI-streaming gate +
  /ai/trips/plan/draft SSE adapter, which the Android DataContainer does not expose as a ready seam
  (AITripPlannerLLMAgentSource requires aiEnabled() + draftPlan()). This page reproduces the canonical
  deterministic baseline the web source itself designates; the agent is out of this unit's scope.

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  The plan stays SI on the wire (meters, seconds, watt-hours). Display conversion happens only at the
  render boundary via TripPlannerDisplayPrefs.distanceDisplay (convertDistanceFromSI) / energy (shared
  formatEnergy) / currency — never stored converted (Phase-48 SI-canonical; ADR-013 keeps cache SI).

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  No SSE live source on this page; planTrip is a one-shot mutation and the vehicle/settings reads are
  cache-then-network Resource streams, so no >2 min live-staleness badge applies (none is a live feed).

DATA STATES (the manifest's declared 3: loading → error → success, for the usePlanTrip source)
  The plan rests at UiPhase.Empty (form only, web `{route && …}` guards) until planTrip runs.

